+# Runtime account-control authority disposition
+
+Status: PROSPECTIVE / NOT EFFECTIVE — exact candidate for owning acceptance/application.
+
+The owner ruling, relayed by the App integration lead on 2026-09-07, is: “I approve this narrow authority amendment.” Its exact decision basis is `projects/chirality-runtime/execution/_Coordination/AgentRuns/RUNTIME_ACCOUNT_LIFECYCLE_PREPARATION_2026-09-07/DECISION_SLATE/DECISION_TEXT.md`, SHA256 `d849f2647170a06f7c7cebc62f41a88cb4d7e96b6d87b23dac3cd8be23c2a64e`. This approves the narrow boundary, not this candidate's exact bytes. The newly reviewed Root D36 candidate is `/Users/ryan/.codex/worktrees/85d6/chirality/execution/_Coordination/AgentRuns/APP_V3_CONSOLIDATED_RESUME_2026-09-07/root/author-v1/D36_PROPOSED_POSTIMAGE.md`, SHA256 `2697862a31ee856ae923c91af38a5e07f8997115a4bd1baabf083afb069939b1`. Its independent review is `/Users/ryan/.codex/worktrees/85d6/chirality/execution/_Coordination/AgentRuns/APP_V3_CONSOLIDATED_RESUME_2026-09-07/root/review-v1/FINAL_PREAPPLICATION_REVIEW.md`, SHA256 `32d44dcc5de4dfc6056ce4e430966f7b46248cd477fc66814f049d08c001d439`, verdict `PASS — READY FOR FAITHFUL CANONICAL APPLICATION`. Parent confirms that candidate was applied locally and remains unpublished; no accepted or published Root main identity was supplied. The Root `APPLIED_UNPUBLISHED` state therefore remains a `PROSPECTIVE / NOT EFFECTIVE` dependency for Runtime and is not effective authority here. This supplement remains `PROSPECTIVE / NOT EFFECTIVE` until exact Runtime acceptance/application, publication/main identity where required for reliance and required Root successor adoption are recorded. SOW propagation then consumes the actual accepted decomposition commit; it is not repinned to an arbitrary later source commit.
+
+## Narrow inherited-contract binding
+
+For DEL-02-09 REQ-001/002 and DEL-02-06 CLM-003, permit a dedicated authenticated account-only authority on the App-facing PUBLIC Runtime HTTP/1.1 Unix API. It is limited to nonexecuting bootstrap authentication, its status/cancellation, and hosted-account lifecycle control/observation. This is an explicit narrow exception to retained project-scoped control wording, not a general nonproject authority. Existing project-scoped authorization remains required for all project operations, including folder disconnect and its result retrieval. An omitted or invented project ID is never authorization. No project access, folder consent, model/tool or no-folder execution, additional user/cloud enrollment, TCP control listener or direct private-supervisor access is granted. DEL-02-07 REQ-006 private supervisor isolation remains unchanged.
+
+DEL-02-06 REQ-010's complete project registration, project-scoped access, requested project/operation authorization, adapter, transport, compatible contract and daemon readiness preconditions remain required before consequential runtime-dependent project work. The nonexecuting account-only operation must instead have its own accepted authenticated caller/operation authority and compatible transport/contract; no such mechanism or completed wire contract is supplied by this boundary disposition. This exception cannot waive project work preconditions through a bootstrap call or broaden the account authority to project operations.
+
+`CUSTODY_DISPOSITION_D36.md` remains immutable. Its accepted D126/D36 intent remains: one sign-in target, independent root authentication and folder consent, no credential copying, custody isolation, global hosted generation fencing, folder-local disconnect, local-model independence, and bounded retirement/revoke/local-cleanup ordering with remote unknown when appropriate. Neither this supplement nor local profile/settings supplies authenticated host identity or supplier qualification. The Root D36 amendment and this later Runtime disposition bind only the added public account-only control boundary.
+
+
+
+## Gates before complete wire acceptance and source activation
+
+| Gate / owning return | Required concrete disposition |
+| --- | --- |
+| Root + Runtime authority | Root records the exact D36 interpretation/amendment under its boundary authority. Runtime SCOPE_CHANGE assesses canonical DEL09 REQ-001/002 and DEL06 implications, applies only an authorized exact candidate, records accepted snapshot, derivative/adoption disposition and affected-client notices. Existing decomposition basis is not repinned merely for a later source commit. |
+| Runtime + App host authority | Specify authenticated recipient delivery, private storage/access, trusted host identity, issuance/validation/revocation, daemon/host generation binding, replacement/exit detection and renderer method allowlist. A local profile, same-UID file mode, broad operator bearer or newly minted token alone is insufficient proof. No mechanism is established by this ruling. |
+| Runtime generation and lifecycle | Specify durable transactions, context admission/fencing inventory, retirement hooks, finite deadlines, late completion/cancellation rules, crash reconciliation and exact internal supervisor operation allowlist. Keep the private supervisor inaccessible to App/CLI. |
+| Runtime + App successor recovery | Define separately who may observe old operation outcomes after account-capability rotation, who may direct cleanup/recovery and what may mutate. Do not restore revoked authority or automatically expose old operations to every newly issued account token. Persisted daemon-owned safe cleanup must not depend on the old caller continuing to poll. Distinguish bounded local cleanup from restarting login or replaying uncertain remote revoke. Exact recipient/operation lineage, disclosure scope and recovery authority remain unresolved; no successor grant is selected here. |
+| Runtime + App consumer contract | Resolve the exact versioned routes, strict schemas/errors, operation ownership/correlation and ceremony/binding/availability projection, including unavailable identity. Preserve corrected project-authorized result retrieval and discriminated start results. Ceremony completion is not hosted readiness. App owns host bridge and UI adoption. |
+| WORKING_ITEMS + independent review | Seal exact source targets, synthetic ports/fixtures, configuration and checks only after the relied contract is accepted. Include rotation/recovery, stale/revoked callers, crash/late completion, bounded cleanup, cross-project denial and strict mixed/secret payload rejection. Review the actual candidate independently before integration. |
+| App + Runtime paired validation | Bind rebuilt and actually running Runtime daemon/client/contracts and App/CLI artifacts. Exercise the accepted journey and unsupported version/error behavior. Earlier stub registration or PR746 CI is not this proof. Live login, OS/backend isolation, exact supplier identity/qualification and release remain separately gated. |
+
+Current production remains unavailable before effects with unavailable binding and hostedReady:false. This ruling cannot enable live start, supplier/build/credential operations, protected-fixture retries, no-folder execution, a new success-identity schema, lifecycle promotion or release. Standing Git authority is unchanged; it supplies neither contract acceptance nor operational authority.
+
+## App journey consequence
+
+Before-folder sign-in can advance to a concrete authenticated host/Runtime design after the narrow ruling; actual ceremony stays unavailable until its prerequisites are met. Folder consent remains independently project-authorized. Folder disconnect and polling use that folder's surviving local control authority. Global sign-out/switch fence hosted generations while preserving local models; exact successor observation and recovery must be settled before adoption. UI must separately show ceremony outcome, unavailable binding, execution availability and incomplete cleanup/remote-unknown results. No sentinel account identity or binary logged-in projection can substitute for those states.
+
+## Conservation and downstream application
+
+SOW-104 remains the single scope item in PKG-02_Runtime_Product; all seven qualified deliverable IDs, four objective IDs, 66 inherited requirement IDs, root-runtime-1 epoch 1, nine holds and separate R16-B disposition remain unchanged. Historical migration/source snapshots, custody supplement, source pins, historical authority hash maps and accepted derivatives are not rewritten. This candidate does not close a deliverable, promote lifecycle or accept new evidence. Derivatives remain to be regenerated or explicitly dispositioned by the owning scope-change workflow. Exact DEL-02-06/09 SOW propagation, Root successor/adoption records and affected App/CLI/client notices remain separate gated outputs; this candidate edits none of them. Canonical publication is not wire or source activation. Standing Git authority remains unchanged.
